<http://data.silknow.org/object/1611898f-bad9-3419-9435-e49e374e1e9a/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "The off-white, plainweave cotton ground is finely quilted with fine wool wadding throughout in white silk thread. The border of scrolling foliage and six-petalled flowers is within two narrow borders of delicately meandering  foliage and star-shaped flowers. The spandrels form a mughal arch and contain flowreing arabesques. The main field is dominated by a large flowering bush. All in chain stitch, in teal blue, sage green, white and pink silk thread, with yellow used in the borders and to delineate the outlines.\nThe Backing: the plainweave cotton is roller-printed with rows of polychrome rows of  long botehs suspended above rose-bearing festoons, against a ground of floral sprigs. Possibly Russian or English.\nThe Facing: the broad facing of bias-cut plainweave cotton is roller-printed with narrow bands containing repeating floral motifs in red, navy blue, yellow and white."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/1611898f-bad9-3419-9435-e49e374e1e9a> .

