        rdfs:comment                   "embroidered & quilted, 1800s, Persian"@en , "The off-white, plainweave cotton ground is finely quilted with fine wool wadding throughout in white silk thread. The border of scrolling foliage and six-petalled flowers is within two narrow borders of delicately meandering  foliage and star-shaped flowers. The spandrels form a mughal arch and contain flowreing arabesques. The main field is dominated by a large flowering bush. All in chain stitch, in teal blue, sage green, white and pink silk thread, with yellow used in the borders and to delineate the outlines.\nThe Backing: the plainweave cotton is roller-printed with rows of polychrome rows of  long botehs suspended above rose-bearing festoons, against a ground of floral sprigs. Possibly Russian or English.\nThe Facing: the broad facing of bias-cut plainweave cotton is roller-printed with narrow bands containing repeating floral motifs in red, navy blue, yellow and white."@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/1d88e706-40b0-33d1-91ee-f5b935f6be57> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/d13829b3-c711-3a62-982c-57ec43d95540> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/4a3e73b4-7fdf-3ea0-a109-ff9aa07a0e13> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/c9634b37-f8c8-3439-8c8b-2471582a4e56> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "embroidered & quilted, 1800s, Persian"@en , "The off-white, plainweave cotton ground is finely quilted with fine wool wadding throughout in white silk thread. The border of scrolling foliage and six-petalled flowers is within two narrow borders of delicately meandering  foliage and star-shaped flowers. The spandrels form a mughal arch and contain flowreing arabesques. The main field is dominated by a large flowering bush. All in chain stitch, in teal blue, sage green, white and pink silk thread, with yellow used in the borders and to delineate the outlines.\nThe Backing: the plainweave cotton is roller-printed with rows of polychrome rows of  long botehs suspended above rose-bearing festoons, against a ground of floral sprigs. Possibly Russian or English.\nThe Facing: the broad facing of bias-cut plainweave cotton is roller-printed with narrow bands containing repeating floral motifs in red, navy blue, yellow and white."@en ;
